{"diagnosis": "Loopback sent 0xa5 with divider 64 but recv_buf_data latched 0xe0, causing tohost FAIL 0xdead TRAP mismatch. States 2-10 advance when recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) (=4) instead of full cfg_divider, sampling ~16x too fast versus state 1 half-bit wait using 2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider. Root cause is the erroneous >>4 divide on cfg_divider in the data/stop timing checks at lines 90 and 97.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (0x1), loopback recv 0xa5 match want 0xa5 with no uart data mismatch TRAP"}

